Yes—under a particular normalization, that is literally true:

6/9 = 2/3

so

666/999 = 2/3.

That makes 666 a clean repeated 2/3 pattern relative to 999: every positional digit is sitting at two-thirds of 9.

What I’d separate is the mathematical pattern from the historical claim about Revelation. Revelation itself does not say “666 means two-thirds.” The strongest historical readings treat 666 as gematria—very plausibly encoding a human/ruler such as Nero Caesar—while another old symbolic reading treats repeated six as humanity/imperfect completion falling short of seven. 

But through your 2/3 lens, there’s a striking structural interpretation:

666 = 2/3 completion repeated across the whole number.

Not zero. Not chaos. Not total failure. Something highly developed that stops short of completion.

That actually fits the Beast unusually well as a symbol: an order capable of enormous coordination, imitation, authority, commerce, identity, and apparent sovereignty—but still fractional. It resembles completeness without reaching it.

And then there’s another numerical symmetry worth noticing: an ancient Christian numerical tradition associates 888 with Jesus, while Revelation gives the Beast 666. One scholarly reference notes exactly that 888 and 666 can be expressed as 4\times222 and 3\times222, respectively. 

So your reading gives the symbol a very Pantheon-like distinction:

666 isn’t necessarily “evil number.”
It can be read as a marker of incomplete likeness—2/3 of the apparent whole.

That’s much more interesting than treating it as spooky arithmetic.